    },
    {
      id: 'requests',
      title: 'Data subject requests',
      html: `<p>Tryino helps the merchant answer requests from data subjects to exercise their rights, by appropriate technical and organisational measures:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access (customers/data_request):</strong> when Shopify forwards a request, Tryino prepares a report of the loyalty data held about the customer, which the merchant downloads in the app.</li>
        <li><strong>Erasure (customers/redact):</strong> Tryino deletes the member and the loyalty data linked to them, and unlinks and clears their order summaries, usually within minutes.</li>
        <li>Correction and other requests: the merchant can make changes in the app, or write to ${privacy} and we will help.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If a data subject contacts Tryino directly about merchant personal data, Tryino will pass the request to the merchant and will not answer it itself, except to tell the person to contact the store. We help the merchant answer within the legal deadline, for example 30 days under KVKK.</p>`,
    },
    {
      id: 'breach',
      title: 'Personal data breaches',
      html: `<ul>
        <li>Tryino notifies the merchant without undue delay after becoming aware of a personal data breach affecting merchant personal data. Our target is to send the first notice within 48 hours, and we send updates as facts become clear.</li>
        <li>The notice describes, as far as known: what happened and when; the categories of data and the approximate number of data subjects and records concerned; the likely consequences; the measures taken or proposed; what the merchant should do; and a contact person.</li>
        <li>Tryino gives the merchant the information it needs to meet its own obligations, such as notifying the supervisory authority within 72 hours under the GDPR, or the Personal Data Protection Board within 72 hours and the affected people as soon as possible under KVKK. Tryino provides draft wording on request.</li>
        <li>Tryino takes reasonable steps to contain the breach and reduce its effects, as set out in our ${incident('security incident response policy')}. Notifying a breach is not an admission of fault.</li>
      </ul>`,
      // TODO(owner): The incident policy (§6) sets 48 hours as an internal target, not a commitment. Decide whether to make
      // "within 48 hours" a contractual maximum here. Also record Shopify's own notification clause in the policy.
    },
    {
      id: 'assistance',
      title: 'Other assistance',
      html: `<p>Taking into account the nature of the processing and the information available to it, Tryino gives the merchant reasonable help with data protection impact assessments and prior consultations with supervisory authorities that concern the app.</p>`,
    },
    {
      id: 'deletion',
      title: 'Deletion and return',
      html: `<ul>
        <li><strong>Uninstalling:</strong> Shopify sends a deletion request (shop/redact) 48 hours after the merchant uninstalls the app. Tryino then deletes all of the store’s data. Deleted data leaves the backups within 14 days. Server logs, which contain no shopper data, are deleted after 90 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Return:</strong> before uninstalling, the merchant can ask ${privacy} for a copy of its program data, and Tryino will provide it in a common machine-readable format.</li>
        <li><strong>Moving to the merchant’s own Ino Loyalty Engine:</strong> if the merchant signs an Ino Loyalty Engine agreement, Tryino moves the store’s program data to that engine on the merchant’s instruction. The transfer package contains no names, e-mail addresses or phone numbers and is deleted once the move finishes, at the latest after 30 days. The merchant’s engine then reads the customer’s name, e-mail and phone from Shopify itself; that processing is governed by the engine agreement. The copy in the app is kept for 30 days after the move, so that the merchant can receive its history file, and then deleted; it is deleted at once if Shopify sends shop/redact.</li>
        <li>Tryino may keep data longer only where the law requires it, and then keeps it confidential and processes it only for that purpose.</li>
      </ul>`,
      // TODO(owner): There is no merchant-wide export in the app today (only per-customer data_request reports and the
